# Fields: a slope field and the solutions that follow it; then a flow.
title "Following the slopes"
schema axes x=[0,6] y=[-1,4] xlabel="t" ylabel="y"
mark S slope fn={1 - y} label="dy/dt = 1 − y"
Say: "Each little |seg|line is the slope the solution must have at that point."
@seg indicate S
Say: "Start a solution at |zero|zero and follow the slopes."
@zero mark s1 solution of=S from=[0,0]
Say: "Start it |high|higher instead, and it still settles at one."
@high morph s1.from -> [0,3] 2s
Say: "Where would a solution starting at minus one end up?"
